{
  "repo": "ARMOR-NODE-ELECTRICAL",
  "ecosystem": "armor",
  "tagline": "Measures the installation with PZEM meters and holds the interlock for a transfer between two sources; switching is off by default.",
  "description": "The firmware of ARMOR-NODE-ELECTRICAL asks up to 16 PZEM meters over one serial line, publishes what they read with its age, and holds the rules for switching contactors: an interlock that never closes two sources together, orders in two steps and a fault that stays until it is acknowledged. Nothing here switches anything today and nothing has run on a board.",
  "columns": [
    "WHAT IS CONNECTED",
    "THIS FIRMWARE",
    "WHO IT TALKS TO"
  ],
